17. package.json Explained
Field	Meaning
name	Project name (jobconnect-frontend)
version	Project version number (1.0.0)
private: true	Stops the project from being published to npm by accident
type: "module"	Lets you use import/export (ES modules) in all .js files, including vite.config.js
scripts	Shortcuts you run with npm run <name>
dependencies	Packages the project needs
18. Scripts
Command	What it does
npm run dev	Starts the Vite dev server at http://localhost:5173 with instant reload
npm run build	Creates the optimized production files in dist/
npm run preview	Serves the built dist/ folder locally so you can test before deploying
19. Dependencies Explained
Package	Purpose in JobConnect
react, react-dom	Core library and the code that renders it in the browser
react-router-dom	Page routing, public and protected routes, redirects
axios	HTTP calls to the backend, with the JWT interceptor
bootstrap	Ready-made responsive styles (grid, buttons, forms, tables)
vite	Dev server and build tool
@vitejs/plugin-react	Lets Vite handle JSX and Fast Refresh

The ^ before a version (for example ^1.6.7) allows compatible minor and patch updates but not a new major version.

20. Suggested Improvements

Move build tools to devDependencies. vite and @vitejs/plugin-react are only needed to build the app, not at runtime. This is the usual convention:

json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "axios": "^1.6.7",
    "bootstrap": "^5.3.3",
    "react": "^18.2.0",
    "react-dom": "^18.2.0",
    "react-router-dom": "^6.22.3"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@vitejs/plugin-react": "^6.0.2",
    "vite": "^8.0.16"
  }
}

Add a test script for the protected-route exercise:

bash
npm install -D vitest @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom jsdom
json
"scripts": {
  "dev": "vite",
  "build": "vite build",
  "preview": "vite preview",
  "test": "vitest"
}

Vitest also needs test: { environment: "jsdom" } added inside defineConfig in vite.config.js.

21. Using Bootstrap

Import it once in main.jsx, before your own CSS so your styles can override it:

jsx
import "bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css";
import "./styles.css";

Example of Bootstrap classes in a job card:

jsx
<div className="card shadow-sm h-100">
  <div className="card-body">
    <h5 className="card-title">{job.title}</h5>
    <p className="text-muted">{job.location}</p>
    <Link to={`/jobs/${job.id}`} className="btn btn-primary btn-sm">View</Link>
  </div>
</div>
22. Installation Troubleshooting
Problem	Fix
npm install fails with a peer dependency error	Check that the vite and @vitejs/plugin-react versions are compatible; try npm install --legacy-peer-deps only as a last resort
Errors about the Node version	Newer Vite versions need a newer Node than 18. Check Vite’s documentation and update the “Requirements” section of your README to match
Changes not showing	Stop and restart npm run dev
Strange errors after switching versions	Delete node_modules and package-lock.json, then run npm install again
23. Useful Commands
bash
npm install                 # install everything in package.json
npm install axios           # add a package
npm install -D vitest       # add a dev-only package
npm outdated                # see packages with newer versions
npm audit --omit=dev        # check production dependencies for known issues
npm run build && npm run preview   # test the production build locally

